An activation system can manage OS version and syntax differences by abstracting device-specific configurations into a modular design, using feature detection to dynamically adapt commands, and employing OS-version-tailored configuration templates. For instance, a template might look like this for Cisco IOS XE: `template l3vpn_config(device_os_version): if device_os_version == "XE17": "router bgp {{asn}}
 address-family ipv4 unicast
